{# W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action> native host dispatch.

   The call site is lowered ahead of the template by
   `forge::native_action::render` and stored on
   `action.native_action_rendered`, so this macro only places it at the
   caller's indent. This backend's dispatcher hands each action the literal
   whitespace prefix its context needs, which a multi-line body would carry only
   on its first line, so the arg-bearing form outside `sce-static` is ONE line:
   it binds the typed payload with `:=` inside the `if` that checks it is there
   — the same tag check the other five spell as a block. A `sce-static` call
   whose argument can fail is the lines of the `try` block that receives it, and
   each of them takes the indent here. #}
{%- macro emit(action, indent, machine_name, model) -%}
{{ indent }}# W3C SCXML G.7: <sce:action name="{{ action.native_action_name }}">
{% if '\n' in action.native_action_rendered -%}
{% for line in action.native_action_rendered.split('\n') -%}
{{ indent }}{{ line }}
{% endfor -%}
{%- else -%}
{{ indent }}{{ action.native_action_rendered }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
